  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNICEF Child Nutrition Fund 2026-2030</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The CNF was co-created by the UK, the Bill and Melinda Gates Foundation, the Children&#x2019;s Investment Fund Foundation and UNICEF and provides a suite of innovative finance mechanisms for addressing child wasting with the aim of transforming the current financing system, which is unpredictable and unsustainable. The fund aims to reach 230 million children and 70 million women across 23 countries with services for the prevention and early detection of malnutrition and treatment of wasting. help reach 230 million children and 70 million women with nutrition services every year.</narrative>
  </description>
